---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="headshot slide-in-block">
    <Image
      src="/img/headshot.jpeg"
      alt="Tyler Crosse"
      width={300}
      height={300}
    />
  </div>

  <section class="intro slide-in-block">
    <p class="eyebrow">Tyler Crosse</p>
    <h1>Engineer & researcher building reliable, interpretable ML systems.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I apply my background in distributed systems to mechanistic
      interpretability and empirical AI safety. I am currently pursuing an MSCS
      at Georgia Tech and am a research fellow at the Supervised Program for
      Alignment Research (SPAR), where I conduct experiments in model evaluation.
    </p>
    <div class="quick-links">
      <a class="pill" href="/ideas">Writing →</a>
      <a
        class="pill"
        href="https://github.com/tylercrosse"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >GitHub ↗</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="now slide-in-block">
    <h2>Currently</h2>
    <ul class="now-list">
      <li>
        Building a goal-drift evaluation harness for reasoning models as part of the
        SPAR fellowship, instrumenting activation drift alongside behavioral metrics.
      </li>
      <!-- <li>
        Writing interpretability experiment logs and BlueDot eval notes to turn paper
        insights into practical measurement checklists.
      </li> -->
      <li>
        Exploring 2026 roles that compound research engineering skills - ML platform,
        interpretability tooling, or evaluation teams in industry labs, alongside
        fellowship applications.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="philosophy slide-in-block">
    <h2>Research Philosophy</h2>
    <p>
      I care about research that closes the gap between theory and deployment. The most useful work
      shows how models think, fail, or shift over time—and ships alongside the instrumentation
      needed to reproduce those findings.
    </p>
    <ul class="philosophy-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Measurement-first.</strong> Every experiment starts with logging plans, drift
        metrics, and benchmarks so results are traceable instead of anecdotal.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tooling for others.</strong> I treat scripts, dashboards, and documentation as part
        of the artifact so collaborators can rerun or extend the work quickly.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open notes.</strong> Publishing retros, partial results, and dead-ends keeps me
        honest and turns “in-progress” thinking into a resource for the community.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>  

  <section class="journey slide-in-block">
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      I began my career with a degree in
      <strong>Biomedical Engineering</strong> from VCU, where I developed an
      interest in software. I spent nearly a decade in industry, leading
      engineering teams and building robust, maintainable systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      The rapid progress in machine learning, exemplified by models like
      <a
        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaFold"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">AlphaFold</a
      >, motivated me to focus on AI alignment. I returned to academia to build a
      stronger foundation in machine learning and contribute to research on
      making AI systems more understandable, steerable, and trustworthy. My
      graduate studies are focused on combining systems engineering with
      interpretability research.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="experience slide-in-block">
    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item current">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Georgia Institute of Technology</h3>
          <p class="company">
            MS Computer Science <span class="period">| 2024 - 2026</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Specializing in Machine Learning and High-Performance Computing.
            Coursework includes Operating Systems, Machine Learning, High
            Dimensional Data Analysis, Deep Learning, and Reinforcement
            Learning. My research focuses on developing evaluation tooling for
            goal drift and collaborating with AI safety reading groups.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item current">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Supervised Program for Alignment Research (SPAR)</h3>
          <p class="company">
            Research Fellow <span class="period">| 2025</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Working under mentor guidance on mechanistic interpretability
            experiments: building the goal drift evaluation harness, maintaining
            reproducible research logs, and translating BlueDot eval discussions
            into actionable measurement plans.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Knowable</h3>
          <p class="company">
            Lead Software Engineer <span class="period">| 5 years</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Led the core engineering team for a legal knowledge platform, where
            I built event-driven microservices using AWS (Lambda/SQS/SNS),
            OpenSearch, and PostgreSQL. I also improved CI/CD processes,
            reducing deployment time by 40%, and mentored other engineers. This
            role provided me with a strong background in instrumentation and
            measurement.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Rosetta Stone</h3>
          <p class="company">
            Senior Software Engineer <span class="period">| 2 years</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Contributed to the language learning platform that's helped millions
            of people learn new languages. Focused on backend systems and API
            development, working with international teams across multiple time
            zones.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Virginia Commonwealth University</h3>
          <p class="company">BS Biomedical Engineering</p>

          <p class="description">
            Where it all started. Studied the intersection of engineering and
            medicine, but discovered my true passion lay in the computational
            side of solving complex problems.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="interests slide-in-block">
    <h2>What I'm Into</h2>
    <div class="interests-grid">
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🧩 Mechanistic Interpretability</h3>
        <p>
          Sparse autoencoders, circuits, and tools to open up black boxes so we
          can understand and steer models.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🎯 AI Safety & Alignment</h3>
        <p>
          Building systems that are steerable, reliable, and beneficial by
          design.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🛡️ Robustness & Evaluation</h3>
        <p>
          Designing measurement suites for honesty, goal drift, and reasoning
          faithfulness under distribution shift.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🔧 Systems for ML</h3>
        <p>
          Operating systems, distributed systems, and tooling that make ML
          research reliable, scalable, and repeatable.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>📊 Interpretability Interfaces</h3>
        <p>
          Building dashboards, visualization layers, and UX that make internal
          model structure legible to researchers and decision-makers.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>⚡ High-Performance Computing</h3>
        <p>
          Squeezing performance from hardware: GPU kernels, memory hierarchies,
          and distributed training pipelines.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>📚 Learning in Public</h3>
        <p>
          Sharing experiments, mistakes, and processes so others can build on
          them, and so collaborators can spot new angles.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🧬 Computational Biology</h3>
        <p>
          Understanding the biological mechanisms that underlie disease and
          development.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

